WEBVTT

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:04.550
You'll be the Master one day.

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.680
But you won't be the next Master.

00:00:09.230 --> 00:00:13.070
Watching you doesn't excite me.

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.750
Two minutes of memorization time remaining.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:21.230
<i>Oh, crap... It's already time for the third round.</i>

00:00:25.080 --> 00:00:26.500
<i>What did he mean?</i>

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:31.250
<i>What did you mean by that,</i>

00:00:32.240 --> 00:00:33.880
<i>Master Suo?</i>

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.180
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:43.010
<b><i>Chihayafuru 3</i></b>

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:50.040
Verse 9

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:50.040
I recall 
how my
own efforts
were
 in vain

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.120
<i>He's rougher than usual today.</i>

00:01:56.840 --> 00:01:57.870
Hi.

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.060
Are you going home, Suo-san?

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:04.940
Oh, Shinobu-chan. I can
 give you a ride if you want.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:06.600
I'm not leaving yet.

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:10.850
I can't come to Omi Jingu and leave 
without paying my respects.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:02:33.540
Maybe that part of your personality 
is what's keeping you strong.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:36.770
Five wins in a row...

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:40.680
You seem pretty confident 
that you can do it.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.090
What is it that's keeping you going, Suo-san?

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.600
Nothing.

00:02:51.800 --> 00:02:55.590
<i>Liar. As if "nothing" makes you that good.</i>

00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.450
<i>It's not like you're a god.</i>

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.870
Kyoto

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.380
We went from the Golden Pavilion to Ninnaji...

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.740
<b>Chi-chan, look over here!</b>

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:08.750
<b>Chi-chan, hurry!</b>

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.740
Then the class split into groups,
and ours went to Arashiyama,

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:12.990
to see Shigureden,
the museum for the Hundred Poets.

00:03:12.990 --> 00:03:14.740
The Hundred Poets?

00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.710
So somber

00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:16.490
Why'd you pick this place, Horikawa?

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:19.620
I only planned this for my group. 
Why'd you guys come along?

00:03:19.620 --> 00:03:22.020
We figured we couldn't go wrong
 if we followed you.

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:25.050
At least come up with your own routes...

00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:31.280
Chi-chan, isn't this place amazing?

00:03:31.280 --> 00:03:34.470
It has dolls of all the Hundred Poets.

00:03:34.470 --> 00:03:37.520
Even your favorite... Ariwara no Narihira, was it?

00:03:37.870 --> 00:03:39.520
Look, he's right here!

00:03:42.510 --> 00:03:45.530
<i>Taichi, how are your matches going?</i>

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:46.810
<i>Are you winning?</i>

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:49.500
<i>And what about Arata?</i>

00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:51.360
<i>I wonder what round they're on now.</i>

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:54.010
<i>I don't know anyone else in western Japan,</i>

00:03:54.010 --> 00:03:55.980
<i>so I'd need Arata to tell me.</i>

00:03:56.830 --> 00:03:59.060
<i>Well? Are you doing your best,</i>

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:01.350
<i>Arata? Taichi?</i>

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:07.420
The battery!

00:04:07.420 --> 00:04:08.530
Here.

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:11.800
Michiru-chan, why...

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.780
I thought I came on this class trip with you!

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:16.560
Why aren't <i>you</i> here?!

00:04:17.300 --> 00:04:19.870
I don't even know anything 
about the Hundred Poets!

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.600
That's why I brought us here!

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:24.940
Because you know about
 these poems and karuta and all that!

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.200
And I'll never understand them
 if you don't teach me!

00:04:31.470 --> 00:04:34.590
Let's wear junihitoe 
together at Shigureden.

00:04:36.330 --> 00:04:39.910
I'm sorry, Michiru-chan! 
I'm sorry! I was stupid!

00:04:39.910 --> 00:04:43.240
But I don't know that much about 
poems and karuta and stuff!

00:04:42.550 --> 00:04:43.710
Huh?!

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.010
What the heck? Why are they 
having a youth moment here?

00:04:43.710 --> 00:04:46.930
I'm so stupid! Stupid! Stupid! Stupid!

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.340
Who gets that worked up in 
a somber place like this?

00:04:46.010 --> 00:04:48.350
<b>Girls are 
amazing</b>

00:04:48.340 --> 00:04:49.930
O-Okay, I get it!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:53.030
Then we should get Heian costumes.

00:04:53.030 --> 00:04:55.480
We can dress up like royalty! 
Let's go put them on!

00:04:55.480 --> 00:04:56.930
Michiru-chan...

00:04:57.540 --> 00:04:59.360
<i>You're right, Michiru-chan.</i>

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:03.800
<i>I came here to Kyoto for my class trip.</i>

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:07.360
I want to be a high school teacher!

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:11.440
What kind of teacher would I be
if I've never been on a class trip?!

00:05:12.690 --> 00:05:14.060
<i>This is once-in-a-lifetime.</i>

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.940
<i>I'll never have a second chance.</i>

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:21.060
The second floor was so big!

00:05:21.060 --> 00:05:23.680
I have heard that the women's 
championships are held here.

00:05:23.680 --> 00:05:25.830
You should take part!

00:05:25.830 --> 00:05:28.150
Well, with how much it costs to get here...

00:05:28.150 --> 00:05:28.670
Huh?

00:05:29.110 --> 00:05:30.050
It's Kana-chan!

00:05:30.800 --> 00:05:32.810
Kana-chan, your group also came to...

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:34.430
Wait, what's wrong?

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.140
N-Nothing! I'm not crying!

00:05:36.940 --> 00:05:39.690
<b>Waaah</b>

00:05:37.140 --> 00:05:39.690
All of the exhibits are just too amazing!

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:43.840
Especially this reproduction of the 
Tentoku Imperial Palace Poetry Contest!

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.270
Tentoku Imperial Palace Poetry Contest?

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.840
I won't let you tell me 
you don't know about it!

00:05:48.840 --> 00:05:52.530
Yeah, I know about it. It was 
a contest with poems, right?

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:54.030
Ahem.

00:05:54.270 --> 00:05:58.470
Poetry contests were held about
 500 times during the Heian period,

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:02.830
but the most famous one was
the Tentoku Imperial Palace Poetry Contest

00:06:02.830 --> 00:06:05.330
held in the year 960 by Emperor Murakami.

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.250
The judge was Fujiwara no Saneyori,

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:11.090
but it's said that he followed 
the wishes of the emperor.

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:14.860
The twelve top poets of the time 
came together and composed poems

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:18.660
about themes such as mist, cherry blossoms, 
Japanese yellow roses, and love.

00:06:18.660 --> 00:06:21.900
Mibu no Tadamine's "As my love" and Taira 
no Kanemori's "Since I could not hide"

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.030
were composed then, and they were 
the top poems of their time.

00:06:23.650 --> 00:06:27.320
<b>There are several others, of course...</b>

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.370
The judge, the reader, and even the court 
ladies struggled to choose a winner.

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:32.030
<b>Wow
 This is it!
 This is the expansive knowledge 
I wanted to hear!</b>

00:06:29.870 --> 00:06:31.620
When I was young,

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:37.280
I thought that composing love poems 
just for a contest was wrong...

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:36.870
<b>When you
were young?
 Like when?</b>

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.020
I was such a child.

00:06:42.600 --> 00:06:44.040
"Since I could not hide..."

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.920
It's said that Emperor Murakami declared 
the winner by whispering those words.

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:53.500
They were competing with the goal 
of moving people's hearts.

00:06:55.870 --> 00:06:57.420
<i>Competing...</i>

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.940
<i>At the Yoshino Tournament,</i>

00:07:01.940 --> 00:07:04.750
<i>Taichi's feelings were laid bare
right in front of me.</i>

00:07:06.780 --> 00:07:08.880
<i>He was hoping to become the Master?</i>

00:07:08.880 --> 00:07:10.640
<i>I want to beat Chihaya.</i>

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:11.500
<i>No...</i>

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:13.000
<i>I want to beat Chihaya.</i>

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.040
<i>No...</i>

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.440
<i>The reason Taichi isn't on this class trip...</i>

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:18.110
<i>I want to win!</i>

00:07:21.460 --> 00:07:24.210
<i>as my concern this morning is 
as tangled as my black hair</i>

00:07:26.690 --> 00:07:28.130
<i>Mashima-kun...</i>

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:31.630
<i>Koishikawa Shusaku of 
the KU Karuta Society.</i>

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:34.780
<i>With a nimble play style that 
balances offense and defense,</i>

00:07:34.780 --> 00:07:38.150
<i>I was the runner-up in the All Japan 
Championship this past April.</i>

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:39.770
<i>My nickname is Kosaku.</i>

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:42.690
<i>Kosaku-senpai's amazing! 
He's already up by nine!</i>

00:07:42.690 --> 00:07:45.880
<i>Kosaku's been on a roll since 
the beginning of the year.</i>

00:07:45.880 --> 00:07:49.790
<i>Landing that job at the Ohishi Tengudo
Karuta Corporation made a big difference.</i>

00:07:50.330 --> 00:07:51.940
<i>I'm going to be...</i>

00:07:53.380 --> 00:07:57.100
<i>a walking advertisement for Oishi Tengudo!</i>

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:58.080
<b>Company president
 Huh? No one expects you to do that...</b>

00:07:58.970 --> 00:08:00.460
<i>I'm down by ten...</i>

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:04.840
Wasn't that boy the runner-up 
at the Yoshino Tournament?

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:05.960
He's not doing well today.

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:07.760
Against Koishikawa-kun...

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:10.770
He must've tried harder then because he 
was playing someone in his own society.

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:13.010
He's trying to attack, but...

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:16.880
<i>This guy is good.</i>

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.290
<i>But I have to attack! Attack!</i>

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:23.150
<i>Go get cards from his side!</i>

00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:24.820
<i>Yes!</i>

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:28.180
<i>A double fault!</i>

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.290
<i>He did it again!</i>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:30.480
<i>It's kicked in!</i>

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:32.480
<i>Goofsaku!</i>

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.490
<b>Goofsaku</b>

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:34.980
<i>A double fault.</i>

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:39.490
<i>before this short summer 
night fully breaks</i>

00:08:35.160 --> 00:08:39.490
<b>Double Fault 
The player can send two cards,
one for the card they took
and one for the fault</b>

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:39.490
<i>I recall how my own efforts were in vain</i>

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:43.940
<i>It's fine.</i>

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.130
<i>It's fine!</i>

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.880
<i>I'm still me, including my goof-ups!</i>

00:08:52.970 --> 00:08:56.260
<i>The double fault didn't faze him at all.
He's playing more freely now.</i>

00:08:55.880 --> 00:08:58.350
<b>Stupid Goofsaku!</b>

00:08:56.260 --> 00:09:00.980
<i>At the All Japan, he committed twenty faults 
in six rounds and was still the runner-up.</i>

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:02.060
<b>Stupid Goofsaku!</b>

00:09:00.980 --> 00:09:02.890
<i>Even when he goofs up, he's strong!</i>

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:02.890
<b>Stupid Goofsaku!</b>

00:09:03.210 --> 00:09:04.790
<i>He pulled ahead again.</i>

00:09:04.790 --> 00:09:06.070
<i>Eight cards now.</i>

00:09:09.580 --> 00:09:11.190
<i>Mashima-senpai...</i>

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:15.990
<i>He's working hard to be 
what he wants to be!</i>

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:22.100
<i>Me...</i>

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:30.490
<i>as my sleeves are wet with dew</i>

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:36.780
<i>His opponent's defending now.</i>

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:37.790
<i>He was attacking before.</i>

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:43.070
<i>There's a definite difference 
in the number of cards.</i>

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:45.970
<i>So my side </i>will<i> be read!</i>

00:09:47.630 --> 00:09:49.900
<i>I don't want to ditch my offensive karuta.</i>

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:52.010
<i>That's Dr. Harada's karuta.</i>

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:53.370
<i>But...</i>

00:09:54.950 --> 00:09:57.410
It goes without saying, but in my mind...

00:09:57.410 --> 00:10:00.160
Offensive karuta is the way to go!

00:10:00.160 --> 00:10:01.780
R-Right...

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:10.880
But your skilled defense against Murao-kun, 
made possible because you were tired...

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:14.530
It suited you.

00:10:19.040 --> 00:10:20.860
<i>Defensive karuta.</i>

00:10:20.860 --> 00:10:22.930
S-Seven in a row!

00:10:23.570 --> 00:10:25.470
He's just one card behind now!

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.140
<i>So the flower petals are scattered 
like the snow by the passing storm,</i>

00:10:32.140 --> 00:10:35.150
<i>A-A semi-double fault now, of all times?!</i>

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:35.150
<b>Not again, Goofsaku!</b>

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:38.650
<i>My own mistake cost me my lead!</i>

00:10:35.150 --> 00:10:39.150
<b>Semi-Double Fault 
A type of double fault in which the 
faulting player is sent a card that, 
coupled with the one that was taken, 
results in a two-card reduction on
the opponent's side</b>

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:39.150
<b>How embarrassing</b>

00:10:40.610 --> 00:10:42.030
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:10:42.350 --> 00:10:44.320
<i>He's leading for the first time, at 5 to 7!</i>

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:45.320
<i>He can do this!</i>

00:10:45.320 --> 00:10:46.250
<i>He can do this!</i>

00:10:46.250 --> 00:10:47.280
<i>He can do this!</i>

00:10:47.540 --> 00:10:56.490
<i>yet it is I who withers and wilts</i>

00:10:57.810 --> 00:10:59.550
<i>Impassionate gods have never seen</i>

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:01.270
<i>Yes!</i>

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:02.090
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:06.130
<i>Mashima-senpai lost "Impassionate"?</i>

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:07.980
<i>It was on his side again!</i>

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:10.640
<i>My switch between offense 
and defense was too slow!</i>

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:11.960
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:11:12.890 --> 00:11:14.110
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:11:14.430 --> 00:11:15.900
<i>Don't let him widen the gap.</i>

00:11:15.900 --> 00:11:16.910
<i>Keep up with him.</i>

00:11:17.630 --> 00:11:18.900
<i>Calm down.</i>

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:20.720
<i>Keep up with him!</i>

00:11:21.410 --> 00:11:22.820
<i>Keep up with him!</i>

00:11:23.280 --> 00:11:24.570
<i>Keep up with him!</i>

00:11:25.050 --> 00:11:26.340
<i>A one-card gap is enough!</i>

00:11:27.490 --> 00:11:30.000
<b>Made it past the first round.
 I'll be the one to represent 
east Japan, so you'd
 better represent the west, Arata.</b>

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.210
<i>They each have one left!</i>

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.960
<b>Long {poem 57}</b>

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:36.960
<b>I feel that {poem 49}</b>

00:11:37.150 --> 00:11:38.320
<i>Luck of the draw...</i>

00:11:39.300 --> 00:11:42.510
<i>I know Arata will win the West Japan Qualifiers.</i>

00:11:44.020 --> 00:11:46.960
<i>I have to win in the east!</i>

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:52.740
<i>Long last we meet...</i>

00:11:56.520 --> 00:11:58.480
Thank you very much.

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.570
Thank you very much.

00:12:02.370 --> 00:12:05.320
He couldn't have helped that. 
It was luck of the draw.

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:07.990
He came within one card of Koishikawa-kun.

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:09.330
That's incredible!

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:12.960
He was so close...

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:23.880
S-Senpai...

00:12:23.880 --> 00:12:25.010
Hanano!

00:12:25.010 --> 00:12:26.400
What, Tsukuba?!

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:27.810
Don't go to him!

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.270
I wouldn't want that.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:31.170
I wouldn't...

00:12:31.860 --> 00:12:34.180
want you coming after me right now!

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:43.220
<i>Gust... A mountain stream... So the flower has...
 After I heard... The hazed early dawn...</i>

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:53.230
<i>The night... The sound of people...
 The sky may... In order for... Said bed...</i>

00:12:47.070 --> 00:12:48.660
<i>I was counting.</i>

00:12:53.230 --> 00:13:05.800
<i>While I... The sight of Mount... May the time...
 Rain... Swift... The sight of the...</i>

00:12:56.990 --> 00:12:58.560
<i>I was counting!</i>

00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:03.140
<i>I counted all of them!</i>

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:08.050
<i>for I could not recognize you, like 
the moon hidden behind the clouds</i>

00:13:08.500 --> 00:13:10.030
<i>The hundredth one...</i>

00:13:10.440 --> 00:13:12.540
<i>It was never read!</i>

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:13.960
<i>And there were no dead cards!</i>

00:13:14.450 --> 00:13:18.010
<i>How was I supposed to get "Long" 
from his side, damn it?!</i>

00:13:23.070 --> 00:13:26.550
<i>Impassionate... on his side...</i>

00:13:23.320 --> 00:13:27.740
<i>the red that is the Tatsuta River</i>

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:29.020
<i>I needed to take that one.</i>

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.770
<i>Just that one!</i>

00:13:30.770 --> 00:13:34.320
<i>No matter where it was... 
even with my eyes closed!</i>

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.600
<i>I'm an idiot.</i>

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:45.130
The male and female semifinal 
competitors have been decided!

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.710
Dr. Harada took down Tamaru-kun!

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:51.790
Dr. Harada!

00:13:52.420 --> 00:13:53.720
We're behind schedule.

00:13:54.190 --> 00:13:56.330
Please take your seats in ten minutes.

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:57.470
That soon?!

00:13:59.600 --> 00:14:00.840
Bathroom...

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.900
Harada-san, where are you?

00:14:17.900 --> 00:14:19.250
You need to get to your spot.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.000
Harada-san?

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:23.150
Hey!

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:25.120
Just wait until he comes out.

00:14:25.120 --> 00:14:26.380
But there's no time...

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:29.670
You can't rush the human body! 
It's ready when it's ready!

00:14:29.670 --> 00:14:31.930
Don't be so stingy over a minute or two!

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:32.990
But...

00:14:32.990 --> 00:14:34.700
He's right, Tsutsumi-kun.

00:14:33.810 --> 00:14:35.390
Huh?

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.120
Give him a minute.

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:38.420
No one's going to complain.

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:38.560
Huh?

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:39.520
Yeah.

00:14:50.700 --> 00:14:57.080
From: Hanano Sumire 
The line-up for the semifinals is set. 
Dr. Harada vs. Koishikawa-san 
Tsuboguchi-san vs. Sudo-san 
Yamamoto-san vs. Sakurazawa-san 
Inokuma-san vs. Yamashiro-san

00:15:01.280 --> 00:15:04.260
<i>Dr. Harada's knees can't take any more.</i>

00:15:04.260 --> 00:15:07.000
<i>His students are picking 
up his cards for him.</i>

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:10.590
<i>I'll be fine. As long as 
I stay calm, I'll be fine.</i>

00:15:10.590 --> 00:15:12.910
<i>Even if I goof up, I'll be fine.</i>

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.850
<b>Whew</b>

00:15:15.030 --> 00:15:20.170
<i>I'm sure Koishikawa-kun has 
never experienced knee pain.</i>

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:25.510
<i>At this point, I can't remember the times 
when my knees didn't hurt.</i>

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.020
<i>That's right.</i>

00:15:29.180 --> 00:15:32.020
<i>I'm good friends with this body by now.</i>

00:15:32.780 --> 00:15:34.750
<i>The sky is the road home...</i>

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:34.750
Whoops!

00:15:35.030 --> 00:15:37.290
<i>He swung at nothing!</i>

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:41.150
<i>But he ended up in a position that looks 
like he's guarding against Koishikawa-kun.</i>

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.600
<i>Wow...</i>

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.790
<i>Dr. Harada isn't falling behind Kosaku-kun.</i>

00:15:56.490 --> 00:16:01.360
Eyelashes, you've been going for the 
opponent's side in luck-of-the-draw matches.

00:16:01.360 --> 00:16:02.370
Why is that?

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:06.660
I once prayed that I wouldn't mind if my side
wasn't read in a luck of the draw ever again.

00:16:08.910 --> 00:16:11.940
Oops, sorry about that! 
But I didn't touch anything!

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.950
It's like he's tempting me into moving

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.950
Dead card

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:15.570
<i>You might not believe it, but...</i>

00:16:15.900 --> 00:16:19.090
<i>When you spend a lot of time 
concentrating in practice,</i>

00:16:19.090 --> 00:16:24.360
<i>you can kind of tell which cards
aren't going to be read.</i>

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:28.340
<b>What?</b>

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:25.080
<i>What?</i>

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.330
<i>The few people who can tell 
call them the "Eternal Maids."</i>

00:16:25.170 --> 00:16:28.340
<b>Heh heh heh heh heh</b>

00:16:28.630 --> 00:16:30.130
Yes! Gotcha!

00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:30.850
<i>He got inside?!</i>

00:16:31.230 --> 00:16:33.050
<i>And since you're able to tell...</i>

00:16:33.130 --> 00:16:34.800
<i>my body burns like the seaweed 
drying on the shores of Matsuho</i>

00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.570
<i>you can spend the second half preparing.</i>

00:16:39.730 --> 00:16:41.330
<i>Kosaku has one card left!</i>

00:16:41.330 --> 00:16:42.860
<i>Dr. Harada has four.</i>

00:16:42.860 --> 00:16:44.910
<i>Don't be Goofsaku again now!</i>

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:50.850
<i>You send the cards that won't 
be read to your opponent...</i>

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:55.390
<i>in preparation for luck of the draw.</i>

00:16:56.910 --> 00:16:58.860
<i>He didn't know?</i>

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:04.800
<i>The look Harada gets on his face when his 
opponent has one card left is pure madness.</i>

00:17:05.490 --> 00:17:07.430
<i>But in truth...</i>

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:11.060
<i>he's calmer than anyone else.</i>

00:17:13.100 --> 00:17:14.790
<i>Luck of the draw...</i>

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.990
<i>It's down to the luck of the draw!</i>

00:17:17.300 --> 00:17:18.800
<i>that you pine for me as the Inaba 
mountain pines, I shall return to you</i>

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.800
<i>my body burns like the seaweed 
drying on the shores of Matsuho</i>

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:26.800
<i>widening into a river
as it descends Mount Tsukuba.</i>

00:17:21.660 --> 00:17:22.590
<i>Be his!</i>

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:24.600
<i>Be Dr. Harada's card!</i>

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:25.730
<i>Be his!</i>

00:17:25.840 --> 00:17:26.820
<i>Be his!</i>

00:17:27.390 --> 00:17:28.780
<i>Be his!</i>

00:17:31.100 --> 00:17:33.420
<i>Note that though...</i>

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.210
<i>Eyelashes, the cards that aren't read</i>

00:17:37.870 --> 00:17:40.620
<i>my body burns like the seaweed 
drying on the shores of Matsuho</i>

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:41.220
<i>are never, ever read.</i>

00:17:49.810 --> 00:17:53.380
<i>A luck-of-the-draw match isn't about luck.</i>

00:17:55.980 --> 00:18:00.220
<i>When you spend a lot of time 
concentrating in practice,</i>

00:18:00.220 --> 00:18:03.390
<i>you can kind of tell which cards
aren't going to be read.</i>

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.260
<i>And I've spent a lot of time...</i>

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.690
<i>To be exact, 45 years.</i>

00:18:10.390 --> 00:18:12.150
Dr. Harada did it!

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:15.040
He really hung in there against 
such a strong young player!

00:18:15.660 --> 00:18:17.610
That's no big deal.

00:18:17.610 --> 00:18:19.780
Don't underestimate a guy 
just because he's older.

00:18:19.780 --> 00:18:22.940
<i>That's right. Youth isn't 
everything in karuta.</i>

00:18:27.350 --> 00:18:28.820
<i>Is Tsuboguchi-kun...</i>

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:37.180
The final round in the East Japan 
Master qualifiers will be

00:18:37.180 --> 00:18:38.850
Harada-san versus Sudo-kun.

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.100
The final round in the 
Queen qualifiers will be

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:44.190
Inokuma-san versus Yamamoto-san.

00:18:44.600 --> 00:18:46.350
We will begin in ten minutes.

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:57.540
<i>I saw these people at 
the summer tournament.</i>

00:18:58.610 --> 00:19:00.610
<i>Who's going to make it all the way to me?</i>

00:19:01.630 --> 00:19:05.420
<i>And I'm pretty sure
she's from the Myojo Society.</i>

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.030
<i>Wataya-kun's down to one card</i>

00:19:10.030 --> 00:19:12.450
<i>against Takemura-kun, the guy 
who beat him last year.</i>

00:19:13.680 --> 00:19:15.590
<i>He's solid this year!</i>

00:19:16.710 --> 00:19:18.480
<i>That's not like Arata.</i>

00:19:18.860 --> 00:19:20.940
<i>He's leading seven cards to one,</i>

00:19:20.940 --> 00:19:23.580
<i>and he's pushing himself to 
go for his opponent's cards?</i>

00:19:26.220 --> 00:19:28.640
<b>Gurgle Gurgle</b>

00:19:28.630 --> 00:19:30.220
I'm sorry.

00:19:31.040 --> 00:19:33.140
<i>Crap. I'm starving.</i>

00:19:33.500 --> 00:19:36.390
<i>Arata'll still win the final round, 
even if he's not at his best.</i>

00:19:36.390 --> 00:19:37.890
<i>I'll just go.</i>

00:19:37.890 --> 00:19:39.120
Shinobu-chan!

00:19:40.150 --> 00:19:41.640
Coach Ise.

00:19:41.640 --> 00:19:43.600
You were watching the semifinals?

00:19:43.600 --> 00:19:45.890
What did you think of our Yuikawa?

00:19:46.270 --> 00:19:50.170
She's a college first-year,
 and her game's been improving lately.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:51.540
<b>Growl</b>

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:56.550
<b>Gurrrrrrgle</b>

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:54.980
What's wrong? You're hungry?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.550
Nah, I'm fine.

00:19:57.910 --> 00:20:02.270
I know I've asked before, but why don't 
you come to a Myojo Society practice?

00:20:02.270 --> 00:20:05.560
Oh, no. All I ever do is get in the way.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:08.670
Mrs. Wakamiya was worried about you.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:11.850
She was saying her granddaughter 
didn't have any friends.

00:20:13.930 --> 00:20:16.360
How about our Yuikawa?

00:20:16.360 --> 00:20:19.270
I think she'd be a great 
practice partner for you.

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:20.780
Even if I crush her?

00:20:23.730 --> 00:20:25.780
W-Wait, Shinobu-chan!

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:29.070
Take this.

00:20:33.030 --> 00:20:34.310
Shinobu-chan!

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:37.650
Feel free to contact me anytime!

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:45.180
<i>It's none of your business.</i>

00:20:46.340 --> 00:20:48.250
<i>None of your business!</i>

00:20:50.430 --> 00:20:52.480
<b>Snowmaru Dorayaki</b>

00:20:56.170 --> 00:20:57.480
Arata-kun!

00:20:58.230 --> 00:20:59.740
Just one more!

00:20:59.740 --> 00:21:00.460
Yeah.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:03.190
I wonder who your opponent 
in the finals will be!

00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:04.890
What's this?

00:21:05.930 --> 00:21:08.530
Oh, that's info on the 
East Japan qualifiers.

00:21:08.530 --> 00:21:12.790
<i>East Japan Semifinals

00:21:09.070 --> 00:21:12.100
I heard everything up through the 
semifinals on the phone earlier.

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:15.060
<i>Taichi didn't make it.</i>

00:21:19.610 --> 00:21:21.190
<i>Why did I just sigh?</i>

00:21:23.460 --> 00:21:24.900
Murao-kun!

00:21:25.420 --> 00:21:27.210
The finalists are decided!

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:30.220
It's Murao Shinichi versus Wataya Arata!

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:34.280
It's a final between Nagumo Society members!
